    <string name="einr_autostart_titel">Start Panoptes when the car is switched on</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_text">For Panoptes to run by itself every time you switch on, it needs a tick in the BYD app management. BYD resets this tick after every car update. Panoptes reminds you then.</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_anleitung">How to: tap “Open settings”. Panoptes tries to set the tick itself. If that does not work, find “Panoptes” in the list and turn on autostart. Then come back here.</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_knopf">Open settings</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_ok">Autostart is on.</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_fehlt">Autostart is still off.</string>
    <string name="einr_autostart_spaeter">I\'ll do it later</string>
    <string name="einr_ueberlagerung_titel">Display over other apps</string>
    <string name="einr_ueberlagerung_text">For Panoptes to show hints (e.g. a charging stop) over the navigation, it needs the “Display over other apps” permission.</string>
    <string name="einr_rechte_titel">What else Panoptes may do</string>
    <string name="einr_rechte_text">Panoptes has been given these permissions. If one is missing, the related feature will not work.</string>
    <string name="einr_recht_kamera">Camera – for the Guardian</string>
    <string name="einr_recht_standort">Location – for the map, the speed camera country check and charging stations</string>
    <string name="einr_recht_speicher">Storage – for recordings</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_titel">Access for Panoptes (USB debugging)</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_warum">So that Panoptes can keep running in the background and repair itself, it needs a one-time access.</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_popup">Android will now show a window: “Allow USB debugging?”. Tick “Always allow from this computer” there and tap “Allow”.</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_knopf">Request access</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_popup_jetzt">Please tick “Always allow” in the Android window and tap “Allow”.</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_warte">Waiting for access …</string>
    <string name="einr_usb_ok">Access granted, Panoptes is running.</string>
